rmat, then call it inside the positive button's onClick handler before instantiating the Entry object. This keeps the fix localized and avoids changing the Callable interface.\n\nNow I'm implementing the validation logic... I'm implementing validation in the Entry class itself—the cleanest place since that's where Base32 decoding happens. I'll wrap the decode call in a try-catch and throw a descriptive exception if it fails, then handle that exception in ManualEntryDialog when creating the entry. I need to trace through all the Entry constructors to see where Base32 decoding happens and ensure validation catches invalid secrets before they cause crashes during the save operation. I need to reconsider the approach—changing constructors to throw exceptions could break other callers, so I should validate the secret before creating the Entry object. I'll add a static validation method to the Entry class and call it from ManualEntryDialog before attempting to instantiate an Entry, checking that the secret contains only valid Base32 characters. I need to validate the secret before decoding it in the Entry constructor to provide a clearer error message. I'll add a static validation method that checks for valid Base32 characters, then use it to wrap the decoding logic with a try-catch that throws an `IllegalArgumentException` with a descriptive message if validation fails.\n\nNow I'm ready to implement both the validation logic in Entry.java and the calling code in ManualEntryDialog.java. I see the stack trace points to the Entry constructor itself as the crash point, so I need to add validation there and throw a descriptive exception rather than letting the Base32 library fail silently. I'll add a static validation method to Entry.java that checks the secret before decoding, then call it from the constructors to provide a clear error message. Finally, I'll wrap the Entry creation in ManualEntryDialog to catch that exception and display it to the user instead of crashing.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
